course: dictionary
lesson: 11190
title: Wistful: a gentle longing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wistful means sad in a soft, dreamy way. You feel wistful when you long for something you cannot have, or for something that is already in the past. «The two friends, so far from home themselves, had something of wistfulness in their eyes.» They are far from home and miss it, so their eyes show a longing sadness.
explain: Authors use wistful to show a feeling without crying. A «wistful smile» is a little sad and a little thoughtful. To work out the meaning, ask: what is the character missing? The clue is often in the words around the word.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, the Rat feels wistful as the birds fly south. He watches them go and feels a longing, so the word tells you his mood is gentle sadness, not anger or fear.
fact: Wistful means sad and full of longing for something you cannot have, or something that is in the past.
fact: Wistful can also mean thoughtful and dreamy, with a gentle sadness.
fact: «A wistful look» and «a wistful smile» are common phrases in stories.
fact: Wistful is an adjective: wistful, more wistful, most wistful.
fact: Wistful shows sadness quietly, so writers use it when a character feels something deep but does not cry.
exercise: «She gave a wistful smile as the train pulled away.» What does wistful show? | Great excitement | Fast running | *Gentle sadness and longing | Anger and shouting
exercise: Mia says wistful means angry. What does it really mean? | Cross and loud | Running fast | *Sad and longing for something far away | Very hungry
exercise: «The old man had a wistful look as he stared at the photograph of his childhood home.» Find and copy the word that tells you about the look. | *wistful | photograph | childhood | stared
test: «Summer is told as a play, and Willow-herb arrives tender and wistful, like a pink sunset cloud.» What feeling does wistful add to Willow-herb? | *Gentle, dreamy sadness | Surprise and laughter | Hunger | Anger
test: Jayden asks, «Is wistful the same as glum?» What is the best answer? | No, wistful means fast | Yes, they mean exactly the same | No, wistful means very angry | *Close, but wistful is about longing for something you cannot have
exam: In «Willow-herb, tender and wistful, like a pink sunset cloud», which idea does wistful help the reader picture? | Being very hungry | *A soft, dreamy, gentle sadness | Loud noise | Shouting and fighting
